codemap 9
tour claude-hooks
kind flow
author ai
group tooling
note The Claude Code hooks: cargo xtask hook <event>, run by Claude Code around the agent's tool calls and turns. They are the process half of the gate: archlint and the gate say what code is acceptable, the hooks keep the agent on the one way each thing is written. Before a tool runs, edits to the map files are denied with the codemap commands to use instead, and a commit is refused unless the gate is green for the current working copy. After an edit to a .rs file, rustfmt formats it and archlint checks it, and the findings go straight back to the agent, so it fixes a rule the moment it breaks it. When the agent stops, the gate runs and a red gate blocks the stop with its failures; after three identical red runs the session may end, the gate stays red, commits stay refused, and the next session starts with the failures in its context. Hooks are Rust in the same binary rather than shell scripts, so they run wherever the workspace builds. Nothing is reserved for the owner: configuration, CLAUDE.md, the crate graph and the API files are edited like any other file.

